## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design a real-time, compliant ML inference workflow using AWS services and to articulate trade-offs between latency, cost, and privacy.

## Key Concepts
- Serverless streaming (Kinesis Data Streams)
- SageMaker inference endpoints
- DynamoDB with PK and GSI
- Glue Data Catalog and schema evolution
- Privacy controls (KMS, VPC endpoints, encryption in transit, IAM)
- Reliability patterns (DLQ, idempotent processing)
- Cost optimization (batch inferences, autoscaling)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lambda snippet calling SageMaker endpoint
const aws = require('aws-sdk');
const Sage = new aws.SageMakerRuntime();
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const payload = event.records.map(r => r.data).join('\n');
  const res = await Sage.invokeEndpoint({ EndpointName: 'sentiment-intent', ContentType: 'text/plain', Body: payload }).promise();
  return res;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate end-to-end latency and implement backpressure?
- How would you handle schema evolution in Glue when new fields appear in transcripts?

